# Project docs (dhara_storage)

When creating or editing README / AGENTS / `docs/` in this repo, **read and follow the `project-docs` skill first**, then apply the customizations below.

Source **documentation comments**, file headers, and why-comments → global skill **`inline-code-docs`** (not this rule).

## Product intent

Pitch, exclusions, and design lineage: **[AGENTS.md → Product intent](../../AGENTS.md)**. Do not invent a new product story. Do not put Windows.Storage name-drops or war stories in READMEs.

## Publish surfaces

| README | Audience / surface |
|--------|-------------------|
| [`README.md`](../../README.md) | GitHub — product overview, package routing |
| [`src/core/dhara_storage/README.md`](../../src/core/dhara_storage/README.md) | crates.io — Rust runtime |
| [`src/core/dhara_storage_dal/README.md`](../../src/core/dhara_storage_dal/README.md) | crates.io — definitions DAL |
| [`src/bindings/dharastorage-ffi/README.md`](../../src/bindings/dharastorage-ffi/README.md) | Native C ABI (NuGet asset) |
| [`src/bindings/csharp/Dhara.Storage/README.md`](../../src/bindings/csharp/Dhara.Storage/README.md) | NuGet — .NET |
| [`tooling/drot/README.md`](../../tooling/drot/README.md) | DROT submodule — operators |

No folder-container READMEs. Submodule project READMEs follow the same convention.

## Audience map

| Package | Speak to |
|---------|----------|
| `dhara_storage`, `dhara_storage_dal` | Rust |
| `Dhara.Storage` | .NET (native = speed/packaging fact, not a Rust tutorial) |
| `dharastorage-ffi` | FFI integrators; steer .NET users to NuGet |
| `drot` | Operators |

## Exceptions

- `tooling/drot/src/drot_dhara_storage/package/README.md` — internal operator notes; keep short; not the publish layout.
- Do not rewrite `docs/**` as product marketing unless asked.
